s6-4-p5 = prose (cons "The property family can be as simple as a postcondition or as rich as a statement about all executions of the program. The first projection recovers the original source term. An annotation language can include host expressions for paths, equivalences, higher inductive objects, or transformations of source syntax; these expressions have the host's expressive power because they are host terms. Their association with a source construct is a type-indexed relation, not an invention of a separate proof language." nil)
